<title>USA: Moore-Handley says White resigns as CEO.</title>
<headline>Moore-Handley says White resigns as CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moore-Handley Inc said Thursday that Emery White has resigned as president and chief executive officer, and the company has named William Riley, chairman, to the additional position of chief executive officer.</p>
<p>The company did not name a president.</p>
<p>Moore-Handley said it has also named Harold Gaines as senior vice-president and chief operating officer. Gaines was formerly vice-president of merchandising.</p>
<p>No reason was given for the resignation.</p>
</text>
